      "observed": "BookEndedRead try-locks the tree, then the run, and releases them in reverse order. While waiting, CommandWait takes the tree lock back with a blocking call and then takes the run lock without blocking. Because the supervisor holds the run lock only while it holds the tree lock, a waiter that resumes is serialised behind the supervisor's tree lock and cannot fail its run-lock reacquire because of the supervisor. A busy lock returns no error from BookEndedRead. Collecting launches writes no run.json, so a waiting build or check is not disturbed (CommandWait compares only run.json). Only booking a fresh read rewrites run.json, which triggers the designed UNIT_WAIT_RETRY and the one reread in work review."
